question.text:
Compute the gradient of the function $f: \mathbb{R}^3 \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ defined by<br>\[
f(\mathbf{x}) = \mathbf{x}^T
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & 2 & 0 \\
0 & -1 & 1 \\
2 & 1 & 3
\end{bmatrix}
\mathbf{x}
\]<br>with respect to $\mathbf{x}$ at  $\mathbf{x} = \begin{bmatrix}1& 0& -1\end{bmatrix}^T.$

Compute the gradient of the function $f: \mathbb{R}^3 \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ defined by<br>\[
f(\mathbf{x}) = \mathbf{x}^T
\begin{bmatrix}
2 & -4 & 1 \\
1 & 2 & 1 \\
-4 & 1 & 2
\end{bmatrix}
\mathbf{x}
\]<br>with respect to $\mathbf{x}$ at  $\mathbf{x} = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix}^T.$

Compute the gradient of the function $f: \mathbb{R}^3 \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ defined by<br>\[
f(\mathbf{x}) = \mathbf{x}^T
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & 0 & 1 \\
0 & 1 & 0 \\
0 & 0 & 1
\end{bmatrix}
\mathbf{x}
\]<br>with respect to $\mathbf{x}$ at  $\mathbf{x} = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \end{bmatrix}^T.$
